1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,430
To understand how an AI algorithm like V-JEPA perceives the

2
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:10,893
world, we must first shed our biological lens. For a

3
00:00:10,993 --> 00:00:14,357
computer, an image has no shape or vivid emotion. It

4
00:00:14,457 --> 00:00:18,753
is simply a two-dimensional grid of numbers representing the light

5
00:00:18,853 --> 00:00:22,484
intensity of three color channels: Red, Green, and Blue.

6
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:27,137
A tensor of shape H multiplied by W multiplied by 3.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,348
And when we stack these still images along the time axis,

8
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:35,824
we get a video. A three-dimensional block representing the continuous flow

9
00:00:35,924 --> 00:00:39,333
of visual information in the space T multiple H multiple W

10
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:43,628
multiple 3. But this very continuity creates an enormous challenge: How

11
00:00:43,728 --> 00:00:47,742
can a computer understand the deep meaning of millions of constantly

12
00:00:47,842 --> 00:00:51,372
changing numbers without being overwhelmed by noisy details?

13
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:57,610
The answer lies in a natural learning mechanism of our brain: Prediction. If

14
00:00:57,710 --> 00:01:01,736
I cover most of this video block, your brain is not confused at

15
00:01:01,836 --> 00:01:06,123
all. You still know which direction the dog is moving, how the ball

16
00:01:06,223 --> 00:01:10,773
will bounce. You don't need to see every pixel to understand the world.

17
00:01:10,873 --> 00:01:14,113
You only need to grasp the semantics of the motion.

18
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:19,473
That is exactly the philosophy of Self-Supervised Learning: learning by

19
00:01:19,573 --> 00:01:23,264
filling in the blanks. This principle has fueled the resounding

20
00:01:23,364 --> 00:01:26,936
success of large language models by predicting missing words.

21
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,088
But how do we apply this principle to video

22
00:01:30,188 --> 00:01:33,500
most effectively? That is when we need V-JEPA.

